    "description": "Caturus is an integrated natural gas and LNG platform that combines upstream gas production with associated midstream and export infrastructure. Its end markets include LNG buyers, gas marketers, and downstream customers seeking low-emission U.S. natural gas supply linked to export capacity. The operating model is asset-heavy and integrated, spanning production, gathering and related infrastructure, and an LNG export project through Commonwealth LNG rather than a pure asset-light marketing model. Public materials state that the platform had crossed the 600 MMcfe per day threshold by August 2025 and targets 3 Bcfe per day over time, while also advancing the 9.5 mtpa Commonwealth LNG project. Kimmeridge first publicly closed development-capital funding for Commonwealth LNG in August 2023, closed a follow-on control investment in June 2024, and later rebranded SoTex HoldCo as Caturus in August 2025 when Mubadala Energy closed a strategic investment for a 24.1% equity stake.",
